  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The software tool \"stineb/rpmodel,\" developed by Benjamin Stocker from ETH Zurich, has garnered 272 downloads and 1,274 views since its release in 2019. Despite the lack of citations or online mentions, the tool serves as a notable contribution to interdisciplinary fields including medicine, engineering, and computer science.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Released in 2019, \"stineb/rpmodel\" is a software tool authored by Benjamin Stocker, affiliated with ETH Zurich. It is hosted on Zenodo, a well-respected open access repository. While the software currently holds no formal citations, the download and view counts indicate that it has been engaged with by a modest audience, suggesting its practical relevance in the community.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">The tool is characterized by its interdisciplinary applicability, touching upon domains such as medicine, engineering, and computer science. This broad scope underlines its potential to support researchers and professionals working across various sectors. Specifically, the concepts associated with the software suggest utility in areas ranging from engineering drawing to the intersection of archaeology and computational methods.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">As part of its stewardship, \"stineb/rpmodel\" is supported by both open and restricted access policies at Zenodo, ensuring its availability for a diverse user base. Additionally, it features in university libraries, as seen through its listing in WorldCat, which indicates an interest for teaching adoption that could facilitate further educational use and enhance visibility.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">While the lack of citations and online discourse may indicate limited immediate impact within the scholarly community, the download statistics suggest that the software is being utilized actively. Continued engagement with users and integration in related research may facilitate a gradual increase in citation counts, thereby enhancing its long-term influence.</p>",
